ORDINANCE NO. ________

ENTITLED: “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING TITLE 10, VEHICLES AND TRAFFIC,
CHAPTER 10.80, BICYCLES, OF THE CHEYENNE CITY CODE FOR
THE PURPOSE OF REMOVING CERTAIN CHAPTER SECTIONS
RELATING TO BICYCLE LICENSING REQUIREMENTS.”

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, Chapter 10.80, Bicycles, of the Cheyenne City
Code, is hereby amended as set out in this ordinance for the purpose of removing certain chapter
sections relating to bicycle licensing requirements.  Existing sections of Chapter 10.80, Bicycles,
not set out in this ordinance remain unchanged.

10.80.090
License required.

No person who resides within this city shall ride or propel a bicycle on any street or upon
any public path set aside for the exclusive use of bicycles unless such bicycle has been licensed
and a license plate is attached thereto as provided under this chapter.

10.80.100
License application.

Application for a bicycle license and license plate shall be made upon a form provided by
the city and shall be made to the city clerk.

10.80.110
License fee.

A license fee of ten dollars ($10.00) shall be paid to the city for new and used bicycles
before a bicycle license is granted. The license will be good for the ownership of the bicycle.

10.80.120
License issuance.

A.  The city clerk upon receiving proper application therefor is authorized to issue a bicycle
license.

B.  The city clerk shall not issue a license for any bicycle when he or she knows or has
reasonable grounds to believe that the applicant is not the owner of or entitled to the possession
of such bicycle.

C.  A merchant who sells bicycles as part of his or her business may collect the license fee at
his or her place of business on the bicycles he or she sells or services, subject to the regulations
adopted by the city clerk. The merchant shall keep a record of each license he or she collects and
shall, within ten (10) days, turn the license fees over to the city clerk together with the
information indicated in subsection D of this section.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
D.  The city clerk shall keep a record of the number of each license, the date issued, the
name and address of the person to whom issued, and the number on the frame of the bicycle for
which issued, and a record of all bicycle license fees collected by him or her.

10.80.130
Attachment of plate.

A.  The city clerk upon issuing a bicycle license shall also issue a license plate bearing the
license number assigned to the bicycle, the name of the city, the calendar year for which issued,
and the expiration date thereof.

B.  The license plate shall be firmly attached to the rear mudguard or frame of the bicycle
for which issued in such position as to be plainly visible from the rear.

C.  No person shall remove a license plate from a bicycle during the period for which issued
except upon a transfer of ownership or in the event the bicycle is dismantled and no longer
operated upon any street in this city.

10.80.140
Inspection.

The chief of police, or an officer assigned such responsibility, may inspect each bicycle
before licensing the same and may refuse a license for any bicycle which he or she determines is
in unsafe mechanical condition.

10.80.150
License renewal.

Upon the expiration of any bicycle license the same may be renewed upon application and
payment of the same fee as upon an original application.

10.80.160
Transfer of ownership.

Upon the sale or other transfer of a licensed bicycle, the licensee shall remove the license
plate and shall either surrender the same to the city clerk or may, upon proper application but
without payment of an additional fee, have the plate assigned to another bicycle owned by the
applicant.

10.80.170
Rental agencies.

A rental agency shall not rent or offer any bicycle for rent unless the bicycle is licensed and
a license plate is attached thereto as provided herein and such bicycle is equipped with the lamps
and other equipment required by the State Vehicle Code.

10.80.180
Bicycle dealers.

Every person engaged in the business of buying or selling new or secondhand bicycles shall
make a monthly report to the chief of police of every bicycle purchased or sold by such dealer,
giving the name and address of the person from whom purchased or to whom sold, a description
```

### Page 3 of 3

```text
of such bicycle by name or make, the frame number thereof, and the number of license plate, if
any, found thereon.

10.80.190 - Violations—Penalties.

IT IS UNLAWFUL FOR ANY PERSON TO VIOLATE ANY OF THE PROVISIONS
OF THIS CHAPTER.  Every person convicted of a violation of any provision of this chapter
shall be fined in accordance with Section 1.24.010 OF CITY CODE. or by removal and
detention of the license plate from such person's bicycle or by the impounding by the chief of
police of such person's bicycle.

Section 2.  That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its approval and publication.

